## SEVERITY / VERDICT
*Blocker:* a path beyond the four; any removed or changed line in a test file; any byte under `src`, `web`, `.github`, a project file; a docs change beyond a pure deletion on line 127 or a word added; a skip, `.only`-style gate, environment gate or sleep in an added row; a lost test name; a non-ASCII byte, ticket key, finding or mutant id, percent figure or person's name in an added test line or message; a secret; **a build warning, a failed or skipped test on the merge ref, or any PR check-run failed or cancelled**; a new open alert; the head moved; a new row red at the head. *Major:* **B562-1 not closed: P8 or P9 survives, or is killed only by an old row**; **B562-2 not closed: P16 survives or is killed only by an old row**; a differential disagreement at the head (or no power under P8, P9, P16); a non-equivalent survivor you cannot prove equivalent; a new row that no mutant turns red and is not a declared control; a builder claim contradicted (5 names, 7 of 7 killed, Import 183, Api 2211); a repeat red; an old killer that no longer dies (a weakened existing row). *Minor/Note:* B562-3 not fully closed by a finer step only (V1h or V1i alive, with the threshold named and shown unreachable or reachable); B562-4 not closed (W5 alive: Minor, as round 1 graded it) ; the case-twin row also killed by an old row (it is a non-regression row); the round-1 Notes not built; the stale comment; B562-6 and B562-7; CI timing; the timing-sensitive Api test passing on rerun. If a closure that round 1 graded Minor stays open, grade it Minor again; if one graded Major stays open, it is Major. Do not soften a Major to avoid the cap; do not harden a Minor to force it.
**ROUND-CAP STATEMENT (binding; copy it into your STATUS verdict section).** This is **round 2 of 2, the cap.** For EVERY finding say whether it is a closed instance of the round-1 class (B562-1 .. B562-5) or a new one. A GO or GO WITH FINDINGS lets Tuesday land #104 once the checks are green (landing rule under Check 7). **A NO GO does not start a round 3: the closed instances stay closed (nothing is reverted; the PR keeps what you proved), the rest is ticketed, and a third round needs the product owner's word** (Tuesday writes the card).

**First line of STATUS:** `GATE VERDICT B580: #104 b560 <GO|GO WITH FINDINGS|NO GO|NOT GATED> @ 006677b (round 2 of 2 - THE CAP - delta <3 commits, 4 paths, +115 -1 y/n; src/web/.github bytes 0 y/n; existing test lines untouched y/n; docs pure deletion on line 127, words added n; names lost n added n> - closure <B562-1 y/n, B562-2 y/n, B562-3 y/n, B562-4 y/n, B562-5 y/n> - rows <5 new, green at the head y/n; red at main's source <names>; each killed by a named new row y/n> - mutants <killed n of m; P8 P9 P16 W5 V1e V1f V1g killed n of 7 by new rows only y/n; survivors <names|none>; equivalents W3 P11 survive y/n; controls c0 c1 c2 c3 cw-weak as expected y/n> - differential <seed 580101, n checks, disagreements n, power P8 n P9 n P16 n> - CI line on the merge ref <Engine n, Import n, Api n, warnings n, failed n> - checks <n completed success of n; pending <names|none>; failing <names|none>> - CodeQL <open alerts n, analyses n of 4> - merge <mergeable, mergeable_state, 3 ahead 0 behind y/n> - lanes sharing a path <n> - gitleaks rc <n>)`. Then the sections: Step 0 (sha256s, slot count), REFUSE counts, PINS (start and verdict, incl. the merge ref and its parents), instrument and load, your predictions (written first), checks 1-9 each with the FAIL clock and evidence path, findings `B580-n` (severity, `path:line` at the head, instrument, FAIL met, closed-instance or new, fix-shape in prose, evidence class MEASURED AT RUNTIME / PROBED / READ ONLY; "none" is valid), the mutant table and the row-kill table, the check-run table with the PENDING set per poll, the ROUND-CAP STATEMENT, FOR TUESDAY (the verdict in plain words; whether #104 can land now and the landing line; "the PR #104 checks are <state>"), FOUND / TESTED / HOW / NOT TESTED / corrections / processes, ports, slots and trees left, **UNMEASURED**. **Last line, exactly:** `VERDICT: B580 #104 b560/mps-importer-source-version-pins @ 006677b <GO|GO WITH FINDINGS|NO GO|NOT GATED> (round 2 of 2, the cap; PR #104 open; CI <complete|pending: names>) on main <sha7>` (main by `ls-remote` at verdict) or `STOPPED: NEEDS TUESDAY <one question>`.
**NOT TESTED BY DESIGN (state each unless you do better):** a browser and the web leg (0 web paths); the hosted site, UAT, demo, production (no HTTP to them); `az`, docker, Kudu, Entra, Graph; Linux and node 24 locally (CI's own jobs are the Linux evidence); real deals, price books and the real catalogue map (never opened: how many real sections end at a map-held code, whether any real map holds two device SKUs differing only in case); CodeQL's queries themselves; a provider matrix (none exists: file-backed and in-memory stores, CI runs one leg); the round-1 Notes; the docs words themselves (the product owner's).

## STANDING LINES
- **SHELL.** Never `cd` (a hook refuses it); absolute single-quoted paths (they hold spaces and `!`); `git -C`; `bash -c` with ARRAYS or a QUOTED heredoc for chains, bash not zsh for loops (zsh does not split an unquoted `$VAR`; write `${VAR}:path`, never `$VAR:path`); no unquoted word that starts with `=`. **A word-split path wrote stray zero-byte files named `=`, `MPS` and `Commercial` into the project root before (they, `seller` and a 6491-byte `head-B104CarePackApiTests.cs` still sit there, and a text file named `Datasec` one level up): CREATE NONE, touch none, never run `python3` or any interpreter on a path that could split; every path in a script is quoted or in an array.** `python3 -I` for anything reading a file you did not write. `/usr/bin/grep -i` with a positive control for every count; every count in STATUS is printed by the command that makes it. Clock from `date`, never typed.
- **Git in the project repo: READ verbs only** (`ls-remote`, `log`, `show`, `diff`, `cat-file`, `ls-tree`, `rev-parse`, `rev-list`, `merge-base`, `grep`, `config` reads, all `--no-optional-locks`) and `fetch` of your refspecs ONLY inside your own clone. FORBIDDEN in the project repo: `fetch`, `pull`, `merge`, `merge-tree --write-tree`, `worktree`, `checkout`, `stash`, `commit`, `reset`, `clean`, `gc`, `prune`. **Never delete** (`mv` to `.tools/b580/quarantine/`); no `rm`.
- **Findings only:** no merge, deploy, Jira write, PR, comment, push, mail, no Artifact/Docs/chat/publish tool, no decision-queue tool in any form (not even `list`), no fleet-ack tool, no scoreboard, no glob over `2_Project_Files/fleet/briefs_staged/`. HTTP only to GitHub GETs under the project's `GH_CONFIG_DIR` and the NuGet restore into your own home. No HTTP to any production or hosted host.
- **No person's name, no decision-card id and no ticket key anywhere in a file you write except STATUS** (say "the product owner"); STATUS carries no person's name either (git author fields hold one: do not quote them). Synthetic data only. 0 non-ASCII bytes in every scratch file and in STATUS (`LC_ALL=C /usr/bin/grep -c '[^ -~]'` = 0; control: a planted raw byte counts 1). STATUS carries no four-underscore run.
- **PRIOR WORK (verify, do not trust):** `git log --oneline 655606a9 -- <each of the four paths>` (the builder: `PanelSectionMapCodeTests.cs` = `949bea7`; the supply file = `ed52643`; the Api white-space file = `655606a`, `5e6a381`), `git log --oneline 655606a9..006677b1`, and a `git grep -n -F` at the head over `src tests` for `PanelRows`, `mapOptionSkus`, `MapHolding`, `SecondDevice`, `CaseTwin`, `ValidatedWithDevicesId`, `INVALID_SUPPLY_PRICE`; the builder says no new name clashes with an existing one and `src` is untouched: a claim that rests on a history that does not say that is a finding.

